  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2010-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Consecutive terms differ by a common difference \\(d.\\) From the last two terms, \\(d=(3p+q)-(3p-q)=2q.\\)\n\nFrom the first two terms, \\(9-p=d=2q,\\) and from the second and third, \\((3p-q)-9=d=2q.\\) Solving this system gives \\(p=5,\\) \\(q=2,\\) and \\(d=4.\\)\n\nThe \\(2010\\)th term is \\[ \\begin{aligned} p+2009d &= 5+2009\\cdot4 \\\\ &= 8041. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "The common difference equals \\((3p+q)-(3p-q)=2q\\)",
        "Also \\(9-p=2q\\) and \\((3p-q)-9=2q;\\) solve for \\(p\\) and \\(q\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
